{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1104846-how-do-you-protect-status-quo-for-the-world","id":1104846,"title":"How do you protect Status Quo for the world?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-17T13:34:31-07:00","id":1104846,"title":"How do you protect Status Quo for the world?","content":"When given godlike power, many players will presumably want to change the mundane world in a way they think is for the better, and quite possibly derail whatever campaign you had in mind for them. For example assassinating world leaders, eradicate dangerous diseases, bring back Firefly, take control of entire countries, destroy Apple.<br /> <br /> Only having read the core rulebook (1st and 2nd Edition) I cannot recall having actually seen much about this topic. It is assumed that mages per default will keep to their cabals and consilia and pursue mysteries all day.<br /> <br /> I am interested to know how you deal with \u200bthese things, or if they have even turned up at all.<br /> <br /> \u200bIf you have a method or cause for stopping players from world-changing feats, how do you go about it?<br /> \u200bIs it because various mage communities will go on a witch-hunt for that audacious mage? Is the God-Machine or the Seers constantly keeping and protecting Status Quo? Will powerful supernatural beings have predicted what the players are about to do and move in early to stop it? Will the very symbols of reality themselves twist the fate of the ambitious mage?<br /> \u200b<br /> Or are things like these happening constantly, and quiessence is keeping us sleepers from sensing that the world is as absurd and twisted as it should be with so many mages and other supernaturals running around?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T13:48:58-07:00","id":1104850,"title":"","content":"Other, more experienced mages have a vested interest in making sure new upstarts don't do this sort of thing.<br /> And, of course, the most powerful 'beings' that can be confirmed to exist in Mage are <i>also</i> very interested in maintaining the status quo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T13:53:47-07:00","id":1104852,"title":"","content":"Mages do try things like that. When they have Gnosis one or two. But, let's be real: when you can twist reality until it breaks, why would you care if Donald Trump or Hillary Clinton is elected president of the United States? What will it change to the fundamental realities of the universe to which you have access? So I consider that most of the things you're talking about, mages just won't do it because they don't care that much. In the same way that Tim Cook COULD totally crash the iPhone of the guy who just mispelled his name at a Starbucks. But he won't, because it's just petty and not worth the trouble. Ancient romans even had a phrase for that: &quot;de minimis non curat praetor&quot;: the judge does not care for trivial things&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12295,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12295-lokiel","user":"Lokiel","date":". 06-17-2017, 04:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12295-lokiel","name":"Lokiel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T13:58:12-07:00","id":1104854,"title":"","content":"Stop them from bringing back firefly? Are you MAD!? :P<br /> <br /> Honestly, in a small group I'd allow changes like these. In larger groups involving more than your standard table of people, anything that involved a status quo would be modified and edited - if not by other mages and supernaturals, then by things like the God Machine and even by the mortals themselves if the mages are not subtle enough. Honestly though, the easiest way to protect the status quo is to occupy their time with other things","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T14:42:57-07:00","id":1104872,"title":"","content":"And, as always, we have things called Exarchs and their Ochemas...<br /> <br /> And then we have all those Seers of Throne <i>actively</i> working for the world to stay the same as Exarchs given them in rule ship.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T15:36:26-07:00","id":1104883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lokiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1104846-how-do-you-protect-status-quo-for-the-world?p=1104852#post1104852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages do try things like that. When they have Gnosis one or two. But, let's be real: when you can twist reality until it breaks, why would you care if Donald Trump or Hillary Clinton is elected president of the United States? What will it change to the fundamental realities of the universe to which you have access? So I consider that most of the things you're talking about, mages just won't do it because they don't care that much. In the same way that Tim Cook COULD totally crash the iPhone of the guy who just mispelled his name at a Starbucks. But he won't, because it's just petty and not worth the trouble. Ancient romans even had a phrase for that: &amp;quot;de minimis non curat praetor&amp;quot;: the judge does not care for trivial things&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mages are human and plenty of the Free Council and Silver Ladder are into political activism in a huge way, possibly to the point that their special dedicated magical tool is &quot;working for a campaign.&quot; And, since the Exarchs use politics to reinforce their control of everything, I can easily see all of them working spells to ensure things go their way.<br /> <br /> If you want to warn the players off of this sort of thing, have an elder tell them about some cabal that used a bunch of magic to try to help Robert Kennedy get elected president and how well that went after all the interference. <br /> <br /> If you want to let them do it, remind them that there's likely a Seer keeping an eye on the big important elections, so they should try their hardest not to leave any traces of themselves on their spells.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T16:10:33-07:00","id":1104888,"title":"","content":"You're right to consider all those factors <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9849_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9849\" data-vbnamecard=\"9849\">Aristarkos</a>. Personally, running assumption is that the 'status quo' that Sleepers uknowingly perceive is partly the result of the myriad cause and effect agendas of mages. Perhaps its too many Acanthi toying with Fate. Or maybe the Ministry of Mammon profits the most from the state of things. What if it's imposed by the Pax Magica of archmages? I see it like a group of children throwing lots of pebbles into the same pond. Each stone makes ripples that make more ripples that encounter other ripples, and the resulting actions are justified by Quiesence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4260-terpsichordean","name":"terpsichordean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4260_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T16:45:27-07:00","id":1104906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1104846-how-do-you-protect-status-quo-for-the-world?p=1104883#post1104883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mages are human and plenty of the Free Council and Silver Ladder are into political activism in a huge way, possibly to the point that their special dedicated magical tool is &quot;working for a campaign.&quot; And, since the Exarchs use politics to reinforce their control of everything, I can easily see all of them working spells to ensure things go their way.<br /> <br /> If you want to warn the players off of this sort of thing, have an elder tell them about some cabal that used a bunch of magic to try to help Robert Kennedy get elected president and how well that went after all the interference.<br /> <br /> If you want to let them do it, remind them that there's likely a Seer keeping an eye on the big important elections, so they should try their hardest not to leave any traces of themselves on their spells.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, true, they do mess with politics. But, imho, they do not care much for the &quot;individual&quot; level of politics but more on its symbolism. For instance, they won't back republicans or democrats or whatever. They will, on a case by case basis, back the political party that further their magical endgoal. For instance, Seers will back the agenda that will further inequality or placidity of the masses, according to their current plan.<br /> <br /> My point was that, as I understand it, mages aren't political militants, at least not for Sleepers parties. They may be, however, militants of supernal causes made manifest in day to day politics. Most of them, and all of the strongest of them, are just simply detached with days to days of mortal life.<br /> <br /> In much the same way, for a mage to bother messing with the minds of TV executives to bring back Firefly because he loves that show would be petty. A mage messing with the minds of TV executives to bring back Firefly because it has some mystical significance is something I can get behind.<br /> <br /> But if it has mystic significance, then it also has mystic opposition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12295-lokiel","name":"Lokiel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T16:45:58-07:00","id":1104907,"title":"","content":"Quiescence stops people remembering Magic, Seers have a vested interest in disrupting the grandiose plans of their compatriots and enemies alike.<br /> And if you really fuck stuff up, there's Time Travel to stop you ever having done it, and the intervention of Archmages and Exarchs to unmake your actions like they never where.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T18:14:24-07:00","id":1104941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aristarkos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1104846-how-do-you-protect-status-quo-for-the-world#post1104846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When given godlike power, many players will presumably want to change the mundane world in a way they think is for the better, and quite possibly derail whatever campaign you had in mind for them. For example assassinating world leaders, eradicate dangerous diseases, bring back Firefly, take control of entire countries, destroy Apple.</div> </div> </div> </div>They'd be drastically overestimating their powers. Assassinating people is easy, but unless your country is the size of 'a small neighborhood' or a population of only a few hundred, you would be out of luck. One could potentially eradicate disease but it would require finding every instance of that disease in the world and destroying it, where you fall into the same pitfalls as groups like the WHO do. It's a lot of work and all it takes is one minor outbreak and one trip to make it so you have to start all over again.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200bIf you have a method or cause for stopping players from world-changing feats, how do you go about it?<br /> \u200bIs it because various mage communities will go on a witch-hunt for that audacious mage? Is the God-Machine or the Seers constantly keeping and protecting Status Quo? Will powerful supernatural beings have predicted what the players are about to do and move in early to stop it? Will the very symbols of reality themselves twist the fate of the ambitious mage? </div> </div> </div>As a ST, if your players want to attempt world-changing feats, they should be encouraged. The game is there for their entertainment as well as your own, and you shouldn't shy away from letting them attempt things like this. It can even have long-lasting repercussions at the table if you play in the same world. If the characters in your Mage game cure AIDS, then in your next game of Vampire AIDS might not exist. But that doesn't mean you should make things easy. Assassinating a world leader would involve various political pitfalls and drawbacks, and then there's the other supernaturals to account for. And considering the length of planning some go into, it's entirely possible that assassination was just part of their plan the whole time. Just like the Lord of the Rings didn't start with Gandalf using Mega-Throw to chuck the ring into the volcano from the Shire, stories your players are in should involve challenges and obstacles.<br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or are things like these happening constantly, and quiessence is keeping us sleepers from sensing that the world is as absurd and twisted as it should be with so many mages and other supernaturals running around? </div> </div> </div>People know about the supernatural, but they don't know the specifics. Even mages don't get the rulebooks, and a lot of them are working off of hope and crossed fingers. But there are magical concerns that affect people aware of magic. It's not just a matter of Quiessence or Lunacy, but these things have an affect on the Integrity of people, and cause the type of Conditions that would make it harder for them to really go out there, be in public and try to get the word out. And even if they did, people know that gazing into the darkness is just a way to get its attention. No one wants to be next.<br /> <br /> In Mage, at least, you do have an entire organization dedicated to making the world an oppressive place, and they're not only masters at dealing with the Pentacle, they have the gods of Mageworld telling them how and when to best act. So while some people may be able to make the world a better place, mages are going to face a direct challenge in their peers. And that's just counting the Seers. You also have people like the Banishers and other members of the Pentacle who would gladly kill you for a variety of reasons, even if your intentions were good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-17-2017, 09:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-19T07:01:52-07:00","id":1105373,"title":"","content":"most of what you described is an useless bullshit, it's a lie and wasting time on affecting it that much is both meaningless and may piss off lots of powerful beings. ON the other hand, 'Status Quo' is already a result of the actions of innumerable parties, supernatural and mundane. <br /> Assassinate World Leaders - Why? it had been done, nothing good came out of it. <br /> Eradicate Diseases - diseases/ e.i microbial cultures serve important role and are interwoven with many beings in many realms. No Thyrsus is dumb enough to even attempt that. <br /> bring back Firefly - so that's why simpsons are still going on... please stop. <br /> take control of entire countries - involves shitton of work that could be better spent on other things and is essentially useless for awakened.<br /> destroy Apple - or any other company that pisses you off driving economy into chaos. GG. <br /> <br /> You want to know what would be a really world changing event done with relatively low arcana? awakening Yellowstone volcano and sending the world to ashen apocalypse.<br /> Or mutating life on global scale, to change ecosystem into something much more inhospitable to humans. <br /> Opening MASSIVE rift to the other-realms. <br /> <br /> Alas, LOTS of very powerful being would be completely against that, so you'll need some serious support up above. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}